    "body": "Seems that BIP433 followed an unconventional path according to BIP3: P2A was [merged on Core](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/30352) in August 2024 and [released in v28.0](https://bitcoincore.org/en/releases/28.0/) in October 2024. The [BIP was proposed](https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/1982) after the fact in September 2025 and merged as Draft in January 2026.\n\n[Rust Bitcoin supports it](https://github.com/rust-bitcoin/rust-bitcoin/pull/4111). [Lightning specs also use this mechanism](https://github.com/lightning/bolts/pull/1228).\n\nWe can [observe that usage has increased since July 2026](https://mainnet.observer/charts/inputs-and-outputs-p2a/).\nThis seems to be related to the [report of abuse of the P2A mechanism](https://delvingbitcoin.org/t/stats-on-compact-block-reconstructions/1052/63).\n\nFor me, that's strong evidence that the BIP is in active use, as per BIP3.",
